{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The movable workbench felt relevant because, like my hand truck, it could help me move equipment and make practical use of my workspace.",
    "The table fits my interest in useful workspace equipment, although I would only consider buying it when I actually need another work surface."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wire connectors, multimeter leads, and battery protector require electrical repair or maintenance needs that I do not currently have; buying screws and washers does not imply those projects.",
    "Grinding bits and the tap kit serve specific machining tasks I have not shown a need for, and the tap's thread size does not match my recent metric screws.",
    "Six recycling bins and a comfort mat do not address my current organizing and fastening needs just because they could belong in a workspace."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My hardware purchases seem to have been taken as a broad interest in electrical repair and specialized tools.",
    "Items that could be used in a garage or workshop seem to have been treated as equally relevant, regardless of the job they solve."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent magnetic hooks, washers, and metric screws point toward hanging, organizing, and fastening things, where the exact function and fit matter.",
    "I rarely choose something without a current use for it; even the relevant workbench would wait until I need a new table."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical workspace equipment but stretched it into repair and machining needs I have not shown."
}"}
